# Drought: "Spells cost an additional "Sacrifice a Swamp" to cast for each black mana symbol in their mana costs." (CR 118.8,
# 601.2f-h). Bot1 casts Drought on turn 1 and pays its upkeep {W}{W} exactly on turns 3 and 5 (Plains and Mox Pearl), so it
# stays. Bot2's Hypnotic Specter ({1}{B}{B}) is refused with one Swamp out on turn 2 (two symbols, two Swamps), though its
# Swamp, Mox Jet and Mox Ruby could pay the mana, while a red Lightning Bolt costs no Swamp. Bot1's own Dark Ritual ({B}) on
# turn 3 takes its one Swamp, tapped for the Ritual's own mana, and then its Duress is refused with {B}{B}{B} floating and no
# Swamp. On turn 6 Bot2, with three Swamps, casts the Specter off all three and sacrifices exactly two of them,
# chosen together in one answer (CR 601.2h).
